    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.28) and **Brice Turang** (75.06) headline our attack as the only players cracking the 75-point threshold. **James Wood** benefits from a premium matchup against Merrill Kelly; his ability to exploit the pitcher's slow delivery, combined with a high-floor leadoff spot and an elite .401 xwOBA, makes him our primary engine for SB and R. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns an elite grade due to the combination of a high-ceiling park factor (+14%) and the opportunity to run against a susceptible battery, cementing his role as a key catalyst. **Seiya Suzuki** (72.03) also emerges as a high-upside play, with favorable wind conditions and a strong platoon edge against the opposing starter pushing his efficiency score well into the top tier.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Alex Freeland** (42.22) in favor of the current starting group. While **Alex Freeland** projected as a viable plug-and-play, his deep-order placement (projected #9) acted as a drag on his raw production, dropping him just below our required 40.0 efficiency threshold to warrant a start. We are closely monitoring the weather in the **Vinnie Pasquantino** (59.39) matchup; while his platoon advantage against the right-handed Matthews is significant, a 38% rain risk introduces variance that could shorten his day. We are also keeping a watchful eye on the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**; both are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and any significant shift in their projected batting order\u2014particularly for **Gabriel Moreno**\u2014could force a late-game pivot to ensure we maximize our daily cap efficiency.",
